    <description>ALF-RS-04 FR10 (rejection side): fires when AF_ApprovalStatus__c changes to Rejected. Hands the trade-in back to the initiating rep and notifies them via email + Custom Notification so they can inform the customer — the pre-existing AF_LossReason__mdt record &quot;Trade_In_Valuation_Not_Accepted&quot; is available if the rep needs to close the deal as lost afterward, but that remains a separate manual action on the Opportunity, not something this flow drives. Real gap found and fixed 2026-09-08 during ALF-RS-04 full-persona-cycle testing (same fix already applied to the sibling AF_FL_Appraisal_ApprovalApproved): the email step used the emailAlert core action (Appraisal.AF_EA_Appraisal_ApprovalRejected, a Workflow EmailAlert) - deployed clean and completed with no fault, but a debug-log capture of a real approval-rejected transition on the Approved-side sibling flow showed ZERO EMAIL_QUEUE entries via that action type, confirmed not proof-of-concept anywhere else in this org either (the one prior EmailMessage that looked similar, for Quote Discount approval, traced to a Workflow alert that turns out not to be referenced by any deployed Flow or ApprovalProcess in this org). Switched to emailSimple (logEmailOnSend=true) instead, matching the proven pattern used everywhere else this session. Updated 2026-09-09: user asked for the customer Contact to also receive this notification, not just the rep. Added Get_Contact (via AF_Contact__c) and Formula_RecipientEmails, same pattern as AF_FL_Appraisal_ApprovalApproved - sends to both rep and Contact when the Contact has an email, falling back to rep-only otherwise.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <name>EmailBody</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>&apos;&lt;html&gt;&lt;body style=&quot;margin:0;padding:16px;background-color:#F4F4F6;font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;max-width:560px;margin:0 auto;background:#FFFFFF;border-radius:6px;border:1px solid #E2E5EA;border-top:4px solid #B3261E;padding:20px 24px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 style=&quot;margin:0 0 12px;font-size:18px;color:#0B2545;&quot;&gt;Trade-In Rejected&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 6px;font-size:14px;color:#4A4A4A;&quot;&gt;The trade-in valuation for &lt;strong&gt;&apos; &amp; {!$Record.AppraisalNumber} &amp; &apos;&lt;/strong&gt; was rejected.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0;font-size:14px;color:#4A4A4A;&quot;&gt;Review the remarks and follow up with the customer.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;&apos;</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>EmailSubject</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>&quot;Rejected: Trade-In &quot; &amp; {!$Record.AppraisalNumber}</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>Formula_RecipientEmails</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>IF(
    ISBLANK({!Get_Contact.Email}),
    {!Get_Rep_ForEmail.Email},
    {!Get_Rep_ForEmail.Email} &amp; &quot;,&quot; &amp; {!Get_Contact.Email}
)</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>NotifBody</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>&quot;The trade-in valuation for &quot; &amp; {!$Record.AppraisalNumber} &amp; &quot; was rejected. Review the remarks and follow up with the customer.&quot;</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>NotifTitle</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>&quot;Trade-In Rejected: &quot; &amp; {!$Record.AppraisalNumber}</expression>
    </formulas>
    <interviewLabel>Appraisal Approval Rejected {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>Appraisal Approval Rejected</label>
